A||||13||KnightRyder31||Mods||||1||
Z||000000||KnightRyder31||10-16-2000||12:26 AM||||Would I notice a diff. if a got performence plugs, wires, and coil? And then got a side scoop, spiral max, and K&N?<BR>Would it be worth it?<BR>I have a 84 Coupe, I want some cheap power.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||10-16-2000||12:44 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KnightRyder31:<BR><B>Would I notice a diff. if a got performence plugs, wires, and coil? And then got a side scoop, spiral max, and K&N?<BR>Would it be worth it?<BR>I have a 84 Coupe, I want some cheap power.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You'd notice an improvement with plugs, if your current ones are old. With new wires and a coil, there would probably be a slight increase in performance but I don't know how much. But don't let me change your mind, I plan on getting platinum plugs, 8.8mm wires and an MSD ignition myself.. hehe.<P>As for a side scoop, spiralmax and a K&N.. I'm not sure. One person I talked to at the GTA Fieros show last month said he did some tests before and after the addition of a holley scoop on the stock intake, and he did get a slight improvement. With a straight pipe to a K&N filter, there'd probably be some improvement.<P>Now.. spiralmax... I've read some articles in Chevy High Performance where a similar device, a Tornado, was tested.. and it did improve the performance of the vehicle.. in fact it took 2/10 of a second off the 1/4 mile time for a modded out S10 truck. I think they do have a 30 day money back guarantee, so you could order it.. get the car dynoed before and after (or just use the ever-popular ass-o-meter) and see if you think it's worth the $60 or however much it costs.<P>Hope this helps!<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000002||BroCar 87||10-16-2000||01:00 AM||||Speaking of Dyno's... we have a couple in Jacksonville, how do I go about getting my fiero dyno'd? Do I have to do anything special? Do I have to have something special?<BR>Whats the deal on dyno's???<BR>Thanks<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature2.jpg"> <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>84 SE (project)||||reg||6
Z||000003||1FST2M6||10-16-2000||08:53 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BlackGTdyno_2.jpg"> <BR>86 GT 4spd...<P>before and after a K&N and 3" aluminum pipe on the intake.. this Dosn't take in to account the air pressue on the car at speed! <P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||JohnnyK||10-16-2000||10:52 AM||||In no way do I believe there is that much HP gain...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||ThatRickGuy||10-16-2000||01:10 PM||||I would. I've seen time sheets and heard tons of people talking about K&N filters. The most scientific explanation I've ever heard is that the K&Ns straighten out air flow at a higher rate. The higher rate beats your stock air intake, and the straightened air flow gets threw the intake easier. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||10-16-2000||02:33 PM||||oh sorry BroCar..  call and set up an appointment. just for a basic base line run session. probly be 3 pulls.. 1 base, one after you change the K&N  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> and an all gear run. $65 at Engineered Performance here in Atlanta. <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  there is no special setup for your car.. you just back it on.. strap it down.. start it up.. roll it out and tighten the straps.. make sure the winPEP software is getting a good tach signal and run it up to 1500 in 4th gear.. the operater of the dyno will say GO you FLOOR the car to redline.. then push in the clutch and lift off the throttle... your done... make a change and do it again.. for an all gear.. he'll say go you ROMP on the car without spinning the tires from a dead stop to redline in EVERY gear... YEAH the 4cyl will do 130+ on a dyno.. there is NO wind resistance. and what ever you do DON'T HIT THE BRAKES IN YOUR CAR WHILE IT'S ROLLING!! you'll end up in a wall... let us know how it goes... take a disk and have theM plot it to a file... so you can post it!<P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||88formula||10-16-2000||06:27 PM||||Here we go again...If you change your plugs, wires and put a higher voltage coil on your fiero you may notice a difference only because your old coil may not provide enough spark above a certain rpm and your old plugs are probably a little worn out. I don’t think it would make a difference on an Iron Duke though because the reline is only 4500 rpm.<P>The K+N filter I don't know but what I have read from numerous articles most cars gain about 1-5 horsepower depending on the engine size and the induction system configuration. Some cars/trucks gain even more horsepower than that but I doubt an Iron Duke would benefit much unless your old filter is getting clogged. I have read in Consumer Reports that a similar contraption called the Tornado is a scam. Consumer Reports tested it on two cars and one lost power and the other gained nothing. I would be real skeptical about putting that thing in your fiero. The fiero’s induction system is a very nonrestrictive induction system. Just doing a tune up on your car would be a benefit power output. The cheapest method of increasing power output would probably be increasing your base timing 2-3 degrees as long as you don't induce detonation. You may have to go with a higher octane fuel after.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 10-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||KnightRyder31||10-16-2000||11:33 PM||||I heard that if I did replace my plugs, wires and coil with high performence ones that it would cause more power flow threw the wires and ignition. Thus, when you floor it, your RPM's will gain much faster. I was wondering if anyone has tried this method.<BR>Its about $105.00 for high per. plugs, wires, coil. $33.00 for K&N. $69.95 for spiralmax. $0-30 for side scoop...would all of this be worth it?||||reg||1
Z||000009||DaRkLoRD||10-17-2000||12:40 AM||||I'd hold off on the spiralmax for now.. get a baseline with the other mods, and then get a spiralmax if you really want.. then, if it doesn't do anything, return it for a refund.. if you add everything all at once, you might assume the spiralmax is adding power, when in fact it might be doing nothing, or even removing power..<P>good luck, and keep us posted on your upgrades!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000010||1FST2M6||10-17-2000||08:27 AM||||you must have been talking to somone that works off commision! yes the wires size makes a difference.. but NOT a noticable difference.. if you take a wire that has 60k miles on it and replace it with a NEW stock replacement you'll be able to show improvment on a dyno but not just changing wire... an if you put ANY splitfire, bosch 4, or Champion "Pro 4" plugs you are covering more of the plug sheilding it making the car NOT use the fuek in the chamber.. the NGK UR5 i had NEVER had a problem with 16+ bottles of nitrous. the spiral-max i have no experiance with.. but <A HREF="http://www.electricsupercharger.com" TARGET=_blank>www.electricsupercharger.com</A>  this works!<P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
